<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Hewlett Packard may add to Irish workforce.</title>
<headline>Hewlett Packard may add to Irish workforce.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. computer group Hewlett Packard may announce a further expansion of its Irish plant in Leixlip and the creation of an additional 1,000 jobs, Irish newspapers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Hewlett Packard is considering a number of its world-wide locations and Irish industrial development agency IDA Ireland is actively pushing Leixlip as an ideal location as the site has plenty of surplus capacity, the reports said.</p>
<p>A decision is imminent and should be made within days or weeks, the newspapers said.</p>
<p>The Irish plant makes ink cartridges for Hewlett Packard printers and currently employs 1,000 people. This number is expected to double by the end of the centry.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
